    ["……你真好，亲爱的，能再帮我做一件事吗？"] = "……You are so kind, my dear. Could you do one more thing for me?",
    ["　　隐匿贤者最初只是一名非人格化的神灵。 \n　　相比起神灵，祂更接近于一种理念，一种自然法则。\n　　信仰祂的摩斯苦修会掌握着“隐者”途径的魔药与晋升方式，成员坚持着道德和戒律，坚持着对知识的追求，并严格守秘。入会者在成为“窥秘人”后，都要禁语五年，学会静默，以便修行和提高专注，甚至是对抗失控。\n　　会内流传着一句格言——为所欲为，但勿伤害——这也为许多“窥秘人”所信奉并践行……贝尔纳黛殿下似乎也很欣赏这句格言。"] = "The Hidden Sage was initially just an impersonal deity. \n Compared to a god, It was closer to a concept, a natural law. \n The Moses Ascetic Order, which believes in It, possesses the potions and advancement methods of the \"Hermit\" pathway. Its members adhere to morality and precepts, persist in the pursuit of knowledge, and strictly maintain secrecy. After becoming a \"Mystery Pryer,\" initiates must remain silent for five years, learning to be quiet in order to cultivate and improve focus, or even to resist loss of control. \n A maxim circulates within the order—Do what you will, but do no harm—which is also believed in and practiced by many \"Mystery Pryers\"... Her Highness Bernadette seems to appreciate this maxim as well.",
